# Frontend Development Rules

## Tech Stack
- Use Next.js 15.3+ for the web application
- Use React 19.1+ for components
- Use TypeScript 5.8+ with strict typing
- Use pnpm for package management
- Use Node.js v22 (via nvm)
- Use React Flow for all node visualization

## Code Organization
- Keep components focused on a single responsibility
- Utilize React hooks for state management
- Implement defensive validation for all data
- Structure components hierarchically for reuse
- Keep components under 400 lines

## UI/UX Guidelines
- Build responsive UIs that work across device sizes
- Implement clear visual hierarchy
- Provide immediate feedback for user actions
- Consider accessibility from the beginning
- Use consistent design patterns

## Testing
- Use Jest and React Testing Library
- Test components in isolation
- Include tests for user interactions
- Test error states and loading states
